      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `TestGeohashUtils_testHashLenToWidth.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/spatial4j/manual/testcases/TestGeohashUtils/TestGeohashUtils_testHashLenToWidth.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test. The key improvements are:\n- Named index constants to clarify what each array element means\n- Descriptive variable names and clearer assertion structure\n- Comments that explain the geohash grid dimensions being testedThe test compiled successfully. The improved version adds named index constants (`LAT_HEIGHT_IDX`, `LON_WIDTH_IDX`) to clarify what each array element represents, a shared `DELTA` constant, and assertion messages that make failures self-explanatory — all without changing the methods called, arguments, or expected values."
    }
  ],
  "last_code": "package org.locationtech.spatial4j.io;\n\nimport org.locationtech.spatial4j.context.SpatialContext;\nimport org.locationtech.spatial4j.shape.Point;\nimport org.junit.Test;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;\n\npublic class TestGeohashUtils_testHashLenToWidth {\n\n    // lookupDegreesSizeForHashLen returns {latHeight, lonWidth}\n    private static final int LAT_HEIGHT_IDX = 0;\n    private static final int LON_WIDTH_IDX  = 1;\n\n    private static final double DELTA = 0.0001;\n\n    SpatialContext ctx = SpatialContext.GEO;\n\n    /**\n     * Verifies geohash cell dimensions against the reference table at\n     * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geohash for both odd-length (3) and\n     * even-length (4) hashes.\n     *\n     * Odd-length (3): the cell is square — 1.40625° × 1.40625°.\n     * Even-length (4): the cell is rectangular — 0.1757° tall × 0.3515° wide.\n     */\n    @Test\n    public void testHashLenToWidth() {\n        // Hash length 3 (odd) produces a square cell\n        double[] oddLenCell = GeohashUtils.lookupDegreesSizeForHashLen(3);\n        assertEquals(\"odd hash len 3: expected lat height ~1.40625°\",\n                1.40625, oddLenCell[LAT_HEIGHT_IDX], DELTA);\n        assertEquals(\"odd hash len 3: expected lon width ~1.40625°\",\n                1.40625, oddLenCell[LON_WIDTH_IDX], DELTA);\n\n        // Hash length 4 (even) produces a rectangular cell (wider than tall)\n        double[] evenLenCell = GeohashUtils.lookupDegreesSizeForHashLen(4);\n        assertEquals(\"even hash len 4: expected lat height ~0.1757°\",\n                0.1757, evenLenCell[LAT_HEIGHT_IDX], DELTA);\n        assertEquals(\"even hash len 4: expected lon width ~0.3515°\",\n                0.3515, evenLenCell[LON_WIDTH_IDX], DELTA);\n    }\n}\n",
